=== Q2
record A { Id: int }
record B { Id: int }

type C = A | B
type C2 = C | A
public atom H(C2 c)
H(c) -> :x
--- stock rc/out:
Q2/m.bs:7:1: error: `{ Kind: :'Q2.A', Id: int }` is absorbed by `{ Kind: :'Q2.A', Id: int } | { Kind: :'Q2.B', Id: int }`
  in C2
  every value of `{ Kind: :'Q2.A', Id: int }` is already a `{ Kind: :'Q2.A', Id: int } | { Kind: :'Q2.B', Id: int }`, so the type declared here
  IS `{ Kind: :'Q2.A', Id: int } | { Kind: :'Q2.B', Id: int }` and the member you wrote is not in it.
  Delete the absorbed member, or narrow the one absorbing it -
  which of those you meant is not something the compiler can tell.
rc=1
